e":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"closed","commit_id":"4ec5b0d6b4d8a57e034b1014942356e95caf47aa","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/commits/4ec5b0d6b4d8a57e034b1014942356e95caf47aa","created_at":"2015-02-02T22:22:01Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/76686023","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/18787#issuecomment-76686023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/18787","id":76686023,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2Njg2MDIz","user":{"login":"borgand","id":103215,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzIxNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103215?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand","html_url":"https://github.com/borgand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-03-02T10:07:07Z","updated_at":"2015-03-02T10:07:07Z","body":"One could argue that it is more correct to set `limit: 8` to **all** SQLite3 `Integer` types, as per: https://www.sqlite.org/datatype3.html:\n\n> INTEGER. The value is a signed integer, stored in 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, or 8 bytes depending on the magnitude of the value.\n> ...\n> If the declared type contains the string \"INT\" then it is assigned INTEGER affinity.\n> ...\n\nThat means that `INT`, `INTEGER`, `TINYINT`, `SMALLINT`, `MEDIUMINT`, `BIGINT`, `UNSIGNED BIG INT`, `INT2`, `INT8` all result in the datatype `INTEGER` and automatic limit up to 8 bytes.\n**NB!**: the documentation does not mention `int4` but it is actually supported in a similar manner.\n\nI would suggest that all integer types that do not explicitly state lower limit (i.e. `int`, `integer`, `int8` and `bigint`) should result in `limit: 8` as otherwise it might break expectations from the field type (with regards to the SQLite3 documentation).\n\nThis is relevant especially in the case where AR is not the creator of the database, thus the type definition might differ from what AR would assume.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/76686023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"borgand","id":103215,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzIxNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103215?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand","html_url":"https://github.com/borgand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/borgand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/116160776","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/18787#issuecomment-116160776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/18787","id":116160776,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExNjE2MDc3Ng==","user":{"login":"inspire22","id":312435,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjQzNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312435?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22","html_url":"https://github.com/inspire22","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inspire22/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-06-27T22:08:30Z","updated_at":"2015-06-27T22:08:30Z","body":"Is there any way to disable range checking?  It doesn't appear to be documented anywhere.\n\nThe feature seems quite prone to bugs, for example \"smallint(5)\" in a mysql database is read as \"limit 2\" for some reason.  The normal size for a smallint is 6, but I'm only storing zip-codes in it so it was 5.  Fixing the database isn't very easy with 20m rows...\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/116160776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"inspire22","id":312435,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjQzNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312435?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co